              "text": "बचावणो (bachāvṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from vañcati, \"moves crookedly; escapes from\". CDIAL lists Old Marwari vacaï under it (CDIAL 11208). It is the causing form of \"to escape\": \"make escape\", so \"save\"; the Old Marwari row means \"is saved\"."
